## Control {{controlId}}: Provide Privacy and Security Notices for CUI

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization provides privacy and security notices consistent with applicable CUI rules within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. System use notifications are presented to users prior to granting access through Azure AD Terms of Use agreements, logon banners, and consent-based access workflows that document user acknowledgment of privacy and security requirements.

{{#if agreementsConfigured}}
Azure AD Terms of Use agreements enforce user acknowledgment of privacy and security obligations. {{agreementsCount}} active agreements are configured, requiring acceptance before CUI system access is granted. Agreements include: system use notification statements, CUI handling requirements per 32 CFR Part 2002, acceptable use policy acknowledgment, and consent to security monitoring. Users must re-accept terms at the frequency defined by organizational policy.
{{else}}
Azure AD Terms of Use agreements have not been configured. Privacy and security notices are delivered through manual onboarding procedures pending automated enforcement.
{{/if}}

{{#if policies}}
Conditional Access policies enforce notice acknowledgment:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires Terms of Use acceptance with {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}.
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Review Azure AD Terms of Use agreement configurations, user acceptance records, and Conditional Access policy enforcement of notice acknowledgment.

